# issue: 602
# red_on: 47abb75f (2026-09-14): step 2 reopen refuses with kind Internal, "OCC recovery sidecar '<opid>' found original commit id '<id>' but its manifest delta differs"
# notes: Two lost writes on one mutation, one seam each: the sidecar confirm put and the post-commit delete, so the `__manifest` commit publishes while the sidecar keeps its arm-time bytes.
# notes: The next read-write open finds the Armed sidecar beside its own visible commit, proves the commit carries the sidecar's planned table version, records one RolledForward audit row, deletes the sidecar, and serves the row.
# notes: Before the heal the reopen refused with kind Internal and every later open refused the same way; the trailing query pins the row the reopen used to hide.

--- runner
timeout_ms: 10000
environments:
  - target: omnigraph-engine-dst
    storage: in-memory-object-store
    seeds: [0]

--- schema
node Person {
    name: String @key
}

--- seed
{"type":"Person","data":{"name":"alice"}}

--- seam
at: mutation.sidecar_confirm_put
occurrence: 1
action: skip
scope: next_step

--- seam
at: mutation.sidecar_post_publish_delete
occurrence: 1
action: skip
scope: next_step

--- mutate
query add_row() {
    insert Person { name: "bob" }
}

--- expect affected: nodes=1 edges=0

--- restart

--- query
query rows_after_reopen() {
    match { $p: Person }
    return { $p.name }
}

--- expect unordered
{"p.name":"alice"}
{"p.name":"bob"}

--- expect shape
p.name: String
